the Democratic Republic of Congo is  facing its deadly deadliest Ebola  outbreak ever the World Health  Organization is warning the disease  could spread to other African countries  making matters worse the DRC's  quarter-century old civil war is  disrupting efforts to treat and contain  the outbreak Debora patta is there this  morning violence and mistrust are  seriously hampering efforts to contain  this outbreak Ebola treatment centers  like this one are often attacked by  militia groups and people are either too  scared or too suspicious to seek medical  help  Ebola is not the only enemy here nine  people were killed in this village by an  armed militia group their soldiers took  the victims to be tested for the disease  it's standard practice Ebola is at its  most contagious immediately after death  we don't understand what the sea bola is  this man says we can bury the bodies of  our people ourselves a 3,000 strong UN  peacekeeping force is deployed in this  area to protect villagers from the over  30 armed militia groups that terrorized  the community you can see how thick and  dense the jungle is here this is where  the militia hide are making it very  difficult to track them and now war  weary residents have to face down  another invisible enemy Ebola community  outreach programs have been launched to  educate people about the virus but  mistrust runs deep USAID's dr. bill  clemmer has worked in the DRC for over  two decades I've never been at a context  where people throw rocks at our  vaccination team where they block roads  where they loot and pillage our health  care facilities Beni has all the tools  to fight Ebola at its disposal but it's  all useless if the sick and the dying  have hide in their homes refusing  medical treatment only 50% of people  infected with Ebola are seeking medical  treatment and they're between 10 to 20  new cases every day the longer this  outbreak rages on the  by the risk of it spreading regionally  and even globally for CBS this morning  Debora patta bene Democratic Republic of  Congo
 

